From fde3959bbba3cd8278ef1a6cb76d5a3b15a7780c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shaurizard <contact@nyoom.engineering>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:53:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] gpu: add gpu_stream_stats to log the command
 processor's draw path

To decide how a host renderer can take over a title's drawing, and to
check afterwards that it sees every draw, the PM4 stream needs to be
measured: how many draws come from the ring and how many from nested
indirect buffers, whether the title replays prerecorded indirect
buffers frame after frame, how much is predicated for tiled rendering,
and how many resolves each frame has.

With gpu_stream_stats set, the command processor counts, on its own
thread, per second: frames, draws by indirect buffer depth (and the
largest frame), draws inside indirect buffers whose address, size and
XXH3 hash were already seen in an earlier frame or earlier in the same
frame, predicated packets and draws, the tile passes per frame (distinct
bin_select values of predicated draws), resolves, draws killed by a
visibility query, and SET_BIN_SELECT, SET_BIN_MASK, EVENT_WRITE_EXT,
VIZ_QUERY and IM_LOAD packets. One line per second goes to
gpu_stream_stats_file. If the executable exports
rex_drawcount_api_counters, its cumulative counters (such as hooked
guest draw function calls) are appended as per-second deltas, so the
draws the title asks for and the draws the GPU receives can be compared
line by line.

When the cvar is off, each packet, indirect buffer, draw and swap pays
one check of a flag that is read once.

Co-authored-by: factory-droid[bot] <138933559+factory-droid[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
